WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.449
How does evidence follow a product from its origin to a business decision?

2
00:00:04.399 --> 00:00:10.245
This page uses three worked structures, not customer case studies, to show the idea.

3
00:00:10.245 --> 00:00:17.928
The coffee chain connects seedlings, farm inputs, processing, export and finance through shared batch records.

4
00:00:17.928 --> 00:00:25.297
The insurance example explains why evidence grades may inform pricing, but cannot predict losses on their own.

5
00:00:25.297 --> 00:00:31.782
The beverage example follows ingredients, factory energy and cold-chain transport across borders.

6
00:00:31.782 --> 00:00:39.230
Together, they show a simple principle: a claim should never reach beyond its boundary or supporting evidence.

7
00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:43.396
A scoped pilot can begin with one product and one decision.
